{"id":"mahabharata-3-048","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":48,"title":"अष्टचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 48 · Sanjaya on the coming war","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra and Sanjaya speak of the Pandavas' growing strength and the kings who rallied to them in the forest, from many lands. Dhritarashtra admits that war is now certain, as Vidura foretold.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರ ಬೆಳೆಯುತ್ತಿರುವ ಬಲವನ್ನೂ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಅವರ ಬಳಿ ಸೇರಿದ ಅನೇಕ ದೇಶಗಳ ರಾಜರನ್ನೂ ಕುರಿತು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಸಂಜಯರು ಮಾತಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ವಿದುರನು ಹೇಳಿದಂತೆ ಯುದ್ಧ ಈಗ ನಿಶ್ಚಿತ ಎಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र और संजय पाण्डवों की बढ़ती शक्ति और वन में उनके पास आए अनेक देशों के राजाओं की बात करते हैं। धृतराष्ट्र स्वीकार करते हैं कि विदुर की भविष्यवाणी के अनुसार अब युद्ध निश्चित है।","te":"పాండవుల పెరుగుతున్న బలం, అడవిలో వారి వద్దకు చేరిన అనేక దేశాల రాజుల గురించి ధృతరాష్ట్ర సంజయులు మాట్లాడుకుంటారు. విదురుడు చెప్పినట్లు యుద్ధం ఇప్పుడు నిశ్చయమని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు ఒప్పుకుంటాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்களின் வளரும் வலிமை பற்றியும், காட்டில் அவர்களிடம் வந்து சேர்ந்த பல நாட்டு மன்னர்கள் பற்றியும் திருதராஷ்டிரனும் ஸஞ்ஜயனும் பேசுகிறார்கள். விதுரர் முன்னுரைத்தபடி போர் இப்போது உறுதி என்று திருதராஷ்டிரன் ஒப்புக்கொள்கிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരുടെ വളരുന്ന ശക്തിയെക്കുറിച്ചും കാട്ടിൽ അവരുടെ പക്ഷത്ത് അണിനിരന്ന വിവിധ ദേശങ്ങളിലെ രാജാക്കന്മാരെക്കുറിച്ചും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രനും സഞ്ജയനും സംസാരിക്കുന്നു. വിദുരൻ പ്രവചിച്ചതുപോലെ യുദ്ധം ഉറപ്പായെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.48; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सुदीर्घमुष्णं निःश्वस्य धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ।\nअब्रवीत्संजयं सूतमामन्त्र्य भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Bharata, Dhritarashtra, son of Ambika, sighed long and hot, and addressed the charioteer Sanjaya."}},{"n":2,"text":"देवपुत्रौ महाभागौ देवराजसमद्युती ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च पाण्डवौ युद्धदुर्मदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two fortunate sons of gods, the Pandava twins Nakula and Sahadeva, radiant as the king of gods, are fierce in battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"दृढायुधौ दूरपातौ युद्धे च कृतनिश्चयौ ।\nशीघ्रहस्तौ दृढक्रोधौ नित्ययुक्तौ तरस्विनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They have firm weapons, shoot far, are resolved in war, quick-handed, firm in anger, ever ready and swift."}},{"n":4,"text":"भीमार्जुनौ पुरोधाय यदा तौ रणमूर्धनि ।\nस्थास्येते सिंहविक्रान्तावश्विनाविव दुःसहौ ।\nन शेषमिह पश्यामि तदा सैन्यस्य संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When those two, fierce as lions and hard to bear like the Ashvins, take their stand at the head of the battle with Bhima and Arjuna in front, Sanjaya, I see nothing of the army surviving."}},{"n":5,"text":"तौ ह्यप्रतिरथौ युद्धे देवपुत्रौ महारथौ ।\nद्रौपद्यास्तं परिक्लेशं न क्षंस्येते त्वमर्षिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two great chariot-warriors, sons of gods, have no equal in battle. Easily angered, they will not forgive Draupadi's humiliation."}},{"n":6,"text":"वृष्णयो वा महेष्वासा पाञ्चाला वा महौजसः ।\nयुधि सत्याभिसंधेन वासुदेवेन रक्षिताः ।\nप्रधक्ष्यन्ति रणे पार्थाः पुत्राणां मम वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether the Vrishnis, mighty bowmen, or the very strong Panchalas, protected in battle by the truthful Vasudeva, the sons of Pritha will burn my sons' army in the fight."}},{"n":7,"text":"रामकृष्णप्रणीतानां वृष्णीनां सूतनन्दन ।\nन शक्यः सहितुं वेगः पर्वतैरपि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even mountains could withstand in battle the onslaught of the Vrishnis led by Rama and Krishna, son of a charioteer's line."}},{"n":8,"text":"तेषां मध्ये महेष्वासो भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ।\nशैक्यया वीरघातिन्या गदया विचरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among them the great archer Bhima of fearsome prowess will range with his iron-studded mace that kills heroes."}},{"n":9,"text":"तथा गाण्डीवनिर्घोषं विस्फूर्जितमिवाशनेः ।\nगदावेगं च भीमस्य नालं सोढुं नराधिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings cannot endure the thunder of the Gandiva, like the crash of a lightning bolt, nor the swing of Bhima's mace."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततोऽहं सुहृदां वाचो दुर्योधनवशानुगः ।\nस्मरणीयाः स्मरिष्यामि मया या न कृताः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, following Duryodhana's will, I will remember the words of friends that I did not follow before and should have recalled."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"व्यतिक्रमोऽयं सुमहांस्त्वया राजन्नुपेक्षितः ।\nसमर्थेनापि यन्मोहात्पुत्रस्ते न निवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you overlooked a very great transgression: though able, you did not restrain your son out of delusion."}},{"n":12,"text":"श्रुत्वा हि निर्जितान्द्यूते पाण्डवान्मधुसूदनः ।\nत्वरितः काम्यके पार्थान्समभावयदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For when Madhusudana Achyuta heard that the Pandavas had been beaten at dice, he hurried to Kamyaka and honored the sons of Pritha."}},{"n":13,"text":"द्रुपदस्य तथा पुत्रा धृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगमाः ।\nविराटो धृष्टकेतुश्च केकयाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So did the sons of Drupada led by Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, Dhrishtaketu and the great chariot-warrior Kekayas."}},{"n":14,"text":"तैश्च यत्कथितं तत्र दृष्ट्वा पार्थान्पराजितान् ।\nचारेण विदितं सर्वं तन्मया वेदितं च ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"What was said there when they saw the Pandavas defeated I learned through spies, and now I tell you."}},{"n":15,"text":"समागम्य वृतस्तत्र पाण्डवैर्मधुसूदनः ।\nसारथ्ये फल्गुनस्याजौ तथेत्याह च तान्हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting there, the Pandavas chose Madhusudana as Arjuna's charioteer in battle, and Hari said, \"So be it.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अमर्षितो हि कृष्णोऽपि दृष्ट्वा पार्थांस्तथागतान् ।\nकृष्णाजिनोत्तरासङ्गानब्रवीच्च युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, too, was furious at seeing the Pritha's sons in such a state, clad in black antelope skins, and he spoke to Yudhishthira."}},{"n":17,"text":"या सा समृद्धिः पार्थानामिन्द्रप्रस्थे बभूव ह ।\nराजसूये मया दृष्टा नृपैरन्यैः सुदुर्लभा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The prosperity that the Pandavas had at Indraprastha, which I saw at the Rajasuya, was very hard for other kings to gain."}},{"n":18,"text":"यत्र सर्वान्महीपालाञ्शस्त्रतेजोभयार्दितान् ।\nसवङ्गाङ्गान्सपौण्ड्रोड्रान्सचोलद्रविडान्धकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There all the rulers of the earth, afflicted by fear of your weapons' power, came, including the Vangas, Angas, Paundras, Odras, Cholas, Dravidas and Andhras."}},{"n":19,"text":"सागरानूपगांश्चैव ये च पत्तनवासिनः ।\nसिंहलान्बर्बरान्म्लेच्छान्ये च जाङ्गलवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Also those living on sea coasts and in the ports, the Sinhalas, Barbaras, mlecchas and dwellers of the dry lands."}},{"n":20,"text":"पश्चिमानि च राज्यानि शतशः सागरान्तिकान् ।\nपह्लवान्दरदान्सर्वान्किरातान्यवनाञ्शकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And hundreds of western kingdoms near the ocean, the Pahlavas, Daradas, all the Kiratas, Yavanas and Shakas."}},{"n":21,"text":"हारहूणांश्च चीनांश्च तुखारान्सैन्धवांस्तथा ।\nजागुडान्रमठान्मुण्डान्स्त्रीराज्यानथ तङ्गणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Haras, Hunas, Chinas, Tukharas, Saindhavas, Jagudas, Ramathas, Mundas, the realm of women and the Tanganas."}},{"n":22,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवो ये च ते भरतर्षभ ।\nआगतानहमद्राक्षं यज्ञे ते परिवेषकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and many others, descendant of Bharata, I saw come as your servers at the sacrifice."}},{"n":23,"text":"सा ते समृद्धिर्यैरात्ता चपला प्रतिसारिणी ।\nआदाय जीवितं तेषामाहरिष्यामि तामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever seized that fickle, shifting fortune of yours, I will take their lives and bring it back."}},{"n":24,"text":"रामेण सह कौरव्य भीमार्जुनयमैस्तथा ।\nअक्रूरगदसाम्बैश्च प्रद्युम्नेनाहुकेन च ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नेन वीरेण शिशुपालात्मजेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Rama, descendant of Kuru, and with Bhima, Arjuna and the twins, with Akrura, Gada, Samba, Pradyumna and Ahuka, with the hero Dhrishtadyumna and Shishupala's son,"}},{"n":25,"text":"दुर्योधनं रणे हत्वा सद्यः कर्णं च भारत ।\nदुःशासनं सौबलेयं यश्चान्यः प्रतियोत्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"having killed Duryodhana in battle, and quickly Karna, Duhshasana, Shakuni's son and whoever else will fight us,"}},{"n":26,"text":"ततस्त्वं हास्तिनपुरे भ्रातृभिः सहितो वसन् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रीं श्रियं प्राप्य प्रशाधि पृथिवीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"you may then live in Hastinapura with your brothers, take the Dhartarashtras' fortune and rule this earth.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अथैनमब्रवीद्राजा तस्मिन्वीरसमागमे ।\nशृण्वत्सु तेषु सर्वेषु धृष्टद्युम्नमुखेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king answered him in that assembly of heroes, while all of them led by Dhrishtadyumna listened."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रतिगृह्णामि ते वाचं सत्यामेतां जनार्दन ।\nअमित्रान्मे महाबाहो सानुबन्धान्हनिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Janardana, I accept this true word of yours. You will kill my foes, great-armed one, together with their followers."}},{"n":29,"text":"वर्षात्त्रयोदशादूर्ध्वं सत्यं मां कुरु केशव ।\nप्रतिज्ञातो वने वासो राजमध्ये मया ह्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But after thirteen years, Keshava, make me true to my word; I vowed to live in the forest, in the midst of the kings.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"तद्धर्मराजवचनं प्रतिश्रुत्य सभासदः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगास्ते शमयामासुरञ्जसा ।\nकेशवं मधुरैर्वाक्यैः कालयुक्तैरमर्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard the word of the king of dharma, the assembly members led by Dhrishtadyumna swiftly calmed the angered Keshava with gentle words suited to the time."}},{"n":31,"text":"पाञ्चालीं चाहुरक्लिष्टां वासुदेवस्य शृण्वतः ।\nदुर्योधनस्तव क्रोधाद्देवि त्यक्ष्यति जीवितम् ।\nप्रतिजानीम ते सत्यं मा शुचो वरवर्णिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"They told the unharmed Panchali in Vasudeva's hearing: \"Lady, Duryodhana will give up his life through your anger. We promise this truly; do not grieve, fair-complexioned one."}},{"n":32,"text":"ये स्म ते कुपितां कृष्णे दृष्ट्वा त्वां प्राहसंस्तदा ।\nमांसानि तेषां खादन्तो हसिष्यन्ति मृगद्विजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who laughed at you when they saw you angry, Krishna, will be laughed at by beasts and birds eating their flesh."}},{"n":33,"text":"पास्यन्ति रुधिरं तेषां गृध्रा गोमायवस्तथा ।\nउत्तमाङ्गानि कर्षन्तो यैस्त्वं कृष्टा सभातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vultures and jackals will drink their blood, those who dragged you by the hair across the assembly floor, while dragging off their heads."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषां द्रक्ष्यसि पाञ्चालि गात्राणि पृथिवीतले ।\nक्रव्यादैः कृष्यमाणानि भक्ष्यमाणानि चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will see their bodies on the ground, Panchali, dragged about and repeatedly devoured by flesh-eaters."}},{"n":35,"text":"परिक्लिष्टासि यैस्तत्र यैश्चापि समुपेक्षिता ।\nतेषामुत्कृत्तशिरसां भूमिः पास्यति शोणितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth will drink the blood of those with severed heads, those who tormented you there and those who looked on and ignored it.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"एवं बहुविधा वाचस्तदोचुः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nसर्वे तेजस्विनः शूराः सर्वे चाहतलक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such many words did those bulls among men speak, all brilliant, brave, and marked by blows from weapons."}},{"n":37,"text":"ते धर्मराजेन वृता वर्षादूर्ध्वं त्रयोदशात् ।\nपुरस्कृत्योपयास्यन्ति वासुदेवं महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chosen by the king of dharma, after the thirteenth year those great chariot-warriors will advance with Vasudeva at their head."}},{"n":38,"text":"रामश्च कृष्णश्च धनंजयश्च\nप्रद्युम्नसाम्बौ युयुधानभीमौ ।\nमाद्रीसुतौ केकयराजपुत्राः\nपाञ्चालपुत्राः सह धर्मराज्ञा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, Krishna, Dhananjaya, Pradyumna and Samba, Yuyudhana and Bhima, the two sons of Madri, the sons of the Kekaya king, and the Panchala princes with the king of dharma."}},{"n":39,"text":"एतान्सर्वाँल्लोकवीरानजेया-\nन्महात्मनः सानुबन्धान्ससैन्यान् ।\nको जीवितार्थी समरे प्रत्युदीया-\nत्क्रुद्धान्सिंहान्केसरिणो यथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man who values his life would face in battle all these great-souled, unconquerable heroes of the world, angry as maned lions, with their allies and armies?"}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"यन्माब्रवीद्विदुरो द्यूतकाले\nत्वं पाण्डवाञ्जेष्यसि चेन्नरेन्द्र ।\nध्रुवं कुरूणामयमन्तकालो\nमहाभयो भविता शोणितौघः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What Vidura told me at the time of the dice game, \"King, if you defeat the Pandavas, this will surely be the Kurus' final hour and a great and terrible flood of blood will come.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"मन्ये तथा तद्भवितेति सूत\nयथा क्षत्ता प्राह वचः पुरा माम् ।\nअसंशयं भविता युद्धमेत-\nद्गते काले पाण्डवानां यथोक्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think it will come about, Sanjaya, just as the counselor said to me then. Without doubt, when the time comes, this war will happen as foretold, with the Pandavas."}}]}]}